<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<PackageManifest Version="2.0.0"
                 xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/vsx-schema/2011"
                 xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/vsx-schema-design/2011">
  <Metadata>
    <Identity Id="Nlabs.ClaudeCodeVsPackage.952c382f-7793-44ac-beab-e4c14cd9470c"
              Version="0.2.0"
              Language="en-US"
              Publisher="Cuma Kose (nLabtech)" />
    <DisplayName>Claude Code for Visual Studio (nLabtech)</DisplayName>
    <Description xml:space="preserve">Runs Claude Code inside Visual Studio.

An agentic chat panel drives the Claude Code CLI, and a native IDE bridge lets Claude see the solution you actually have open - files, the current selection, compiler errors, symbols and the debugger - instead of inferring it from the file system.

Every tool call is graded for risk before it runs, and you allow, deny, or allow it for the session. A proposed edit arrives as a diff, not as raw JSON. What each turn spent - input, output, reasoning and cached tokens, and cost - stays on the turn it belongs to, and the session total is one click away. Dictation, image attachments, subagents and slash commands are built in.

Ships as two assemblies with no third-party dependencies.

Requires the Claude Code CLI and your own Claude account; this extension provides no model access of its own. Independent work, not officially affiliated with Anthropic or Microsoft.</Description>
    <MoreInfo>https://github.com/nlabtech/nlabs-claude-code-vs-package</MoreInfo>
    <License>LICENSE</License>
    <ReleaseNotes>CHANGELOG.md</ReleaseNotes>
    <Icon>icon.png</Icon>
    <PreviewImage>preview.jpg</PreviewImage>
    <Tags>claude, claude code, ai, agent, cli, debugger, productivity</Tags>
  </Metadata>

  <Installation>
    <!--
      Only the LOWER bound of the version range is read; the upper bound is ignored.
      That is why [17.0,) installs a SINGLE VSIX on both Visual Studio 2022 and 2026:
      compatibility is now driven by the API version, not the product version.
    -->
    <InstallationTarget Id="Microsoft.VisualStudio.Community" Version="[17.0,)">
      <ProductArchitecture>amd64</ProductArchitecture>
    </InstallationTarget>
  </Installation>

  <Dependencies>
    <Dependency Id="Microsoft.Framework.NDP" DisplayName="Microsoft .NET Framework"
                d:Source="Manual" Version="[4.7.2,)" />
  </Dependencies>

  <Prerequisites>
    <Prerequisite Id="Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.CoreEditor"
                  Version="[17.0,)" DisplayName="Visual Studio core editor" />
  </Prerequisites>

  <Assets>
    <Asset Type="Microsoft.VisualStudio.VsPackage"
           d:Source="Project" d:ProjectName="%CurrentProject%"
           Path="|%CurrentProject%;PkgdefProjectOutputGroup|" />
  </Assets>
</PackageManifest>
